## Day 11 – SQL CASE Statement

### 📌 Overview

Day 11 focuses on the SQL CASE statement and conditional logic. Practical employee, customer, order, and sales scenarios were used to understand how CASE can be applied to business analysis.

### 📚 Topics Covered

* Basic CASE Statement
* CASE with Multiple Conditions
* CASE with AND and OR
* CASE with JOIN
* CASE with GROUP BY
* SUM(CASE WHEN...)
* COUNT(CASE WHEN...)
* CASE with NULL
* CASE with JOIN and GROUP BY
* Conditional Aggregation
* Business-oriented CASE scenarios

### 💼 Practical Analysis

The practice includes employee salary classification, customer segmentation, order classification, sales categorization, bonus classification, customer priority analysis, missing-data identification, and category-wise conditional aggregation.

### ⭐ Important Data Analyst Concepts

Special focus was given to:

* `SUM(CASE WHEN...)`
* `COUNT(CASE WHEN...)`
* CASE with aggregate functions
* CASE with JOIN
* CASE with GROUP BY
* Conditional aggregation

### 🎯 Learning Objective

The objective of Day 11 was to learn how to use conditional logic in SQL and apply CASE statements to real-world Data Analyst problems.

### 💼 Business Applications

CASE statements can be used for:

* Customer segmentation
* Salary classification
* Sales performance analysis
* Order classification
* Bonus and incentive analysis
* Customer prioritization
* Data quality checks
* Conditional aggregation
* Business reporting

